tres, centred on the part.", "measurement": "opening_at:3.4:mid-32,mid+22", "comparison": "at_most", "threshold": {"magnitude": 0.5, "unit": "mm"}, "source": "user", "type": "geometric", "verification": "exact_geometry", "strength": "hard", "state": "accepted"}, {"id": "REQ_AT_3_4_MIDM32_MIDM22", "statement": "The 3.4 mm opening shall be on a corner of the 64 by 44 mm rectangle of centres, centred on the part.", "measurement": "opening_at:3.4:mid-32,mid-22", "comparison": "at_most", "threshold": {"magnitude": 0.5, "unit": "mm"}, "source": "user", "type": "geometric", "verification": "exact_geometry", "strength": "hard", "state": "accepted"}], "assumptions": [{"id": "ASM_MATERIAL_PLA", "statement": "The plate is manufactured by FDM 3D printing in PLA, as stated, with no specific infill or layer orientation given, so a solid/standard-strength print is assumed sufficient for a non-structural mounting plate.", "rationale": "Brief states '3D-printed PLA' as the process/material.", "consequence_if_wrong": "If a particular infill or wall count is required for stiffness around the cutouts, the default print settings could leave inadequate strength at the cable hole or zip-tie slots.", "risk": "low", "reversible": true, "approved": true}, {"id": "ASM_FC_FRAME_PATTERN_ALIGNMENT", "statement": "The 30.5 mm FC mounting pattern and the 64x44 mm frame mounting pattern are both centred on the plate and aligned with the plate's length/width axes (FC pattern axis-aligned, not rotated 45 degrees as some standards use).", "rationale": "The brief gives both patterns as 'centred on the plate' without specifying rotation; axis-aligned squares/rectangles are the conventional default for this class of part.", "consequence_if_wrong": "If the FC pattern is meant to be rotated 45 degrees (a common FC standoff convention), holes would not align with the physical flight controller.", "risk": "moderate", "reversible": true, "approved": false}, {"id": "ASM_ZIP_TIE_SLOT_ORIENTATION", "statement": "The two zip-tie slots run lengthwise (along the 80 mm dimension), are centred across the 60 mm width, and are placed symmetrically with one slot's centre 14 mm from each end of the plate.", "rationale": "Brief states slots run 'along the plate's length... centred across the width, with their centres 14 mm from each end.'", "consequence_if_wrong": "If the slots are meant to be offset differently or oriented across the width, cable routing geometry would be wrong.", "risk": "low", "reversible": true, "approved": true}, {"id": "ASM_NO_CHAMFER_NO_INSERTS", "statement": "No chamfers, countersinks, or heat-set insert bosses are added at any hole; all holes are plain straight through-holes sized as stated.", "rationale": "The brief gives only hole diameters, with no mention of countersinking or inserts.", "consequence_if_wrong": "If heat-set inserts or countersunk screws are actually intended, the plain holes would not retain fasteners or would allow screw heads to protrude.", "risk": "moderate", "reversible": true, "approved": false}, {"id": "ASM_ORDINARY_INDOOR_SERVICE", "statement": "The plate operates in typical small-drone service conditions (ambient temperature, no sustained exposure above PLA's ~50-60 degC softening point) with no special environmental protection required.", "rationale": "No environmental or duty-cycle information is given in the brief, and PLA is the stated material.", "consequence_if_wrong": "Exposure to heat (e.g., near ESCs or in direct sun in a hot vehicle) could soften or warp the PLA plate.", "risk": "moderate", "reversible": true, "approved": false}]}}